From b6a1e46d640c18b7aac65eb91e041c894398c4cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 16:23:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] Add owl-egl, a client-side EGL-over-CGL library for
 hardware GL

Wayland GL clients under owl have so far rendered through Mesa
swrast into wl_shm buffers. owl-egl is a drop-in libEGL.1.dylib that
renders through CGL (the real GPU) into IOSurface-backed FBOs and
shares them with the compositor over the existing
zowl_iosurface_manager_v1 / zowl_mach_ipc_v1 protocols, whose
compositor half has been waiting for exactly this client.

EGL 1.4, desktop OpenGL only (CGL has no GLES), window surfaces
only, wayland platform only. The client's "framebuffer 0" is the
surface's back FBO: eglMakeCurrent leaves it bound, and clients that
resolve GL through eglGetProcAddress (mpv, SDL2, EGL-built epoxy)
get thin wrappers that remap explicit binds of 0 and the
corresponding glGetIntegerv queries. Buffers (up to 3, lazily
created, resized on acquisition) ride a private wayland event queue;
eglSwapBuffers throttles on wl_surface.frame per the swap interval.
EGL 1.5 entry points exist as failing stubs so binaries linked
against Mesa's libEGL still load with this one substituted.

Plain C, no ObjC and no blocks, -mmacosx-version-min=10.6 (on 10.5
there is no IOSurface; software rendering remains the path there).
Built by its own Makefile, Mac-only: wayland-scanner client code for
the two owl protocols plus MIG user stubs from the same .defs the
compositor builds its server stubs from. Installs into
PREFIX/lib/owl-egl/ so it never collides with Mesa's libEGL; clients
opt in with DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/local/lib/owl-egl (dyld overrides
by leaf name, no relinking).

See HWGL.md at the repository root for the full design, the
compositor survey it rests on, and the testing plan.

